Tab Finder Privacy Policy
Last updated: September 30, 2026
Tab Finder is a browser extension that helps you search, organize, save and back up your open tabs.
What Tab Finder accesses
To work, Tab Finder reads the titles and web addresses of your open tabs, your tab groups, and your windows. When you choose "Bookmark window to folder", it creates bookmarks in your browser.
Where your data is kept
Your saved sessions, backups, settings and window names are stored only on your own computer, in your browser's local extension storage. Tab Finder has no servers. It does not send your data anywhere.
What Tab Finder does not do
It does not collect, sell or share your personal information.
It does not track you or use analytics or advertising.
It does not read the contents of the web pages you visit.
Deleting your data
Removing the extension from your browser deletes everything it stored.
